@startuml
title What is collected today, and what the FIPS asks for

skinparam backgroundColor #FEFEFE
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam ArrowColor #374151
skinparam ArrowThickness 1.3
skinparam rectangle {
  BorderColor #1F2937
  FontColor #111827
}
skinparam note {
  BackgroundColor #F9FAFB
  BorderColor #9CA3AF
}

rectangle "TODAY — `delivery.rs`: a FLAT SET of entries" as NOW #FEE2E2 {
  rectangle "**ESet**" as NOWSET #FEF2F2
  rectangle "EList[ d0, d1, leaf_A ]" as E1 #FECACA
  rectangle "EList[ d0, d2, leaf_B ]" as E2 #FECACA
  rectangle "EList[ d3, d4, leaf_C ]" as E3 #FECACA
  NOWSET --> E1
  NOWSET --> E2
  NOWSET --> E3
}

note bottom of NOW
  Each `d`<i>i</i> is a 32-byte content digest, and the module
  header says why: **"a consumer KEYS on a trace —
  it never destructures one."**

  Consequences:
  • the INPUT EXPRESSION appears nowhere
  • `d0` is stored TWICE — no prefix is shared
  • a trace cannot be walked as a reduction sequence
  • the leaf is APPENDED to a list, not the end of a path
end note

rectangle "PROPOSED — an `EPathMap`: a PREFIX-COMPRESSED TRIE" as NEW #DCFCE7 {
  rectangle "**root**\nthe INPUT EXPRESSION" as ROOT #DBEAFE
  rectangle "redex-node `d0`\n<i>shared by two branches</i>" as D0 #EDE9FE
  rectangle "redex-node `d1`" as D1 #EDE9FE
  rectangle "redex-node `d2`" as D2 #EDE9FE
  rectangle "redex-node `d3`" as D3 #EDE9FE
  rectangle "leaf A\n<i>terminal segment</i>" as LA #DCFCE7
  rectangle "leaf B\n<i>terminal segment</i>" as LB #DCFCE7
  rectangle "leaf C\n<i>terminal segment</i>" as LC #DCFCE7

  ROOT --> D0
  ROOT --> D3
  D0   --> D1
  D0   --> D2
  D1   --> LA
  D2   --> LB
  D3   --> LC
}

note bottom of NEW
  The key is `enc(d0) ‖ enc(d1) ‖ … ‖ enc(leaf) ‖ 0x00`,
  which is **byte-for-byte what the codec already builds**.

  • INTERIOR nodes are the redexes
  • the LEAF EXPRESSION is the terminal segment, before `0x00`
  • branches that fired the same prefix SHARE those bytes
  • interior and terminal are told apart by TAG BYTE:
    `0x06` step · `0x0B` failure · `0x0C` truncated · `0x0F` reified
end note

NOW -[#DC2626,thickness=2]-> NEW : the same entries,\nstored so that the\nSTRUCTURE is preserved

@enduml
